WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:00.750
Good Morning, John.

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.560
I'm sleepy and there's a lot going on and I'm making this video

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.840
substantially ahead of time because PodCon is happening this weekend

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.460
and I will admit that to a certain extent - not with my personal life -

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.520
but with the world at large I've kind of, sorta, I've a little bit had it.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.540
I am feeling grumpy.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.960
And I like to put positive energy out in the world, but also I like to be myself

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.460
and I like to experience the emotions that I'm experiencing and I found in my pocket of this jean jacket

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.300
questions from when we did live Dear Hank and Johns while on tour.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.920
We're gonna do a live Dear Hank and John at PodCon so that's gonna be great.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:31.820
What's this?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.740
This is just a coaster from my hotel. So, I wanted to answer some of these questions,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.290
I don't know if we answered them on tour,

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.309
I don't know why they're in my pocket.

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:41.549
But I will say that these are not necessarily the answers that I would give if I were in a good mood.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.009
I'm very excited from PodCon, very excited to do all the stuff

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.460
I'm doing in my life. My actual life.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.709
Project for Awesome is coming.

00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:48.570
My baby is very cute.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.480
Everything is good in my personal and professional life.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.400
But I don't know if you've heard about the rest of the world...

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.200
All right. Let's do the questions.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.194
"How can you be supportive when a friend of yours gets a haircut you find really weird?"

00:00:59.194 --> 00:01:00.180
All haircuts are weird.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.940
What other organism is like:

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:07.080
"I'm just going to let my hair, let it grow forever. It's gonna get--" it's like imagine a zebra out,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.280
it's like galloping along, tripping over its fur.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.080
People are so weird! Our hair grows forever

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.980
and the only other organisms that do this are freaking...

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.100
...domesticated dogs

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.120
that we bred to have dumb hair.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.080
All haircuts are weird.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.480
"What if, like Dorothy in The Wizard of Oz, I want to believe that there's no place like home,

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.080
but also I don't know exactly where home is?"

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.540
Rachel, welcome...

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.920
...to adulthood.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.600
This is from Lindsey who asked: "What should be the signature dish that I bake to impress new friends?"

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:41.140
Uh, your signature dish-- I mean nachos go in the oven, right? What else do you bake?

00:01:41.146 --> 00:01:43.460
Bake? Bake potatoes, baked potatoes!

00:01:43.466 --> 00:01:44.360
Biscuits and gravy.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.500
Hot... corn dogs. Do you bake corndogs? You bake?

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.800
No, you don't. You fry them.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.240
This is from Anthony: "My brother spends a lot of time at home alone.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.120
I came home to him playing guitar and singing. I didn't know he did either of those things.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.900
I spoiled his secret talent! How do I tell him?"

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.860
Don't tell him! It's his secret! He wants it to be a secret!

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:03.629
He wants to let you guys know in his own time.

00:02:03.629 --> 00:02:09.200
It can be really a lot of pressure at that stage between when you like don't know anything,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.960
and then you start to get kinda good at stuff.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.800
Like there's this huge gap between okay and good

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.020
and you don't know about that gap in the beginning.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.580
'Cause like anybody who could do anything with a guitar is magic if you don't know what's going on.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.520
I would let him...

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:29.420
Practice in peace. Annie says "You're doing very great, sweetie." Thank you. That... that helps.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.620
"This world has a tendency not to be as awesome as it should be.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:33.700
Brothers,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.200
Would you be willing to support me in becoming the world's dictator?"

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.560
Below that it says: "Your loyalty will be rewarded."

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.980
I mean, Dakota, you had me until the end there.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.980
"As a turtle biologist, I must ask: What is your favorite kind of turtle?"

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.520
Um... I don't - I just realized I made a turtle face when I read that. I like sea turtles a lot...

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.580
They're really good. Especially baby ones. I also like Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:58.840
I like turtle men, like Dr. Lawrence Turtleman our least

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.140
popular thing I've done on vlogbrothers...

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.300
maybe ever.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:08.520
"When I write sometimes it feels really stupid and bad writing. When I read it back it's way better than I thought,

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.660
but this makes me question my writing. Does this happen to you?"

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.640
YES!

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.540
It totally does!

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.780
The thing to, like, give credence to is not like, in the moment you're thinking about it

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.320
and you're fixing and breaking and reforming.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.420
It's after you have done that...

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.660
...reading it and how do you feel about that final product not the...

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.900
...terrible mess in between.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.850
"How will I ever know if I've actually succeeded?" -Mica

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.059
Let me tell you, friend, that doesn't happen.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.510
You will never know. You will succeed in individual events,

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:43.980
but failure will always be just around the corner, so find things that sustain you that aren't...

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.800
...imaginary, like friends.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.060
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.740
Also, hey, John, free domestic shipping at dftba.com for the next three days if you order $80 or more.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.380
Yeah

